      {"kind": "line", "from": [67, 118], "to": [91, 118], "stroke": {"color": "accent", "weight": 0.5}},
      {"kind": "text", "flow": "body", "rect": [66, 136, 276, 392], "style": "Verse", "sample": [
        "My grandmother kept the tide tables",
        "pinned above the kitchen sink,",
        "a column of small numbers",
        "she read the way some people read the psalms.",
        "",
        "High water, six fourteen. Low, twelve forty.",
        "She knew when the boats would lift",
        "and when the mud would shine",
        "and when to send us down for cockles,",
        "",
        "and none of it was faith, exactly,",
        "only the long habit of attention,",
        "the moon’s slow arithmetic",
        "done twice a day without complaint.",
        "",
        "I keep them too, now, on my phone,",
        "and still I go down to the water",
        "at the wrong time, mostly,",
        "and wait, as she did, to be corrected."
      ]}
    ]}
